  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Suppose that \\(a \\ast b\\) means \\(3a - b.\\) What is the value of \\(x\\) if \\[2 \\ast (5 \\ast x) = 1?\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\( \\dfrac{1}{10} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\( 2 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\( \\dfrac{10}{3} \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\( 10 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\( 14 \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "10"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2016-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "First, \\(5\\ast x=15-x\\). Applying the operation again gives \\[\\begin{aligned} 2\\ast(15-x)&=6-(15-x)\\\\ &=x-9. \\end{aligned}\\] Thus \\(x-9=1\\), so \\(x=10\\).\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Start by simplifying the inner operation \\(5\\ast x\\).",
        "Apply the definition \\(a\\ast b=3a-b\\) twice, from the inside out."
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
